  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member reading my MPs, I want each one-to-one conversation to show my correspondent's avatar, not a grey placeholder, so that I recognise people at a glance. Operator feedback, 2026-11-07, milestone M4.\n\n### Cause\nOnly the read side of the avatar cache was ported.\n- `MessageAvatarView.swift:10-47` (LOT-126) reads `AvatarCache` (LOT-066) and falls back to a grey circle.\n- Nothing in the app or the engine ever calls `AvatarCache.store` (`git grep AvatarCache`). Every lookup misses, so every avatar is grey.\n- Legacy filled the cache while parsing topic pages: `ParseMessagesOperation.m:176, 430-446` @ 2440d79, downloading when the avatar was missing or older than 24 h.\n\n### Proposal\n1. **Fill the cache from the pages read (parity).**\n   - When a topic or MP page block has an `avatarURL` (`MessageBlockParser.swift:113-120`, `TopicPageSource.swift:84`), hand `(pseudo, url)` to an app-side `AvatarStore` actor.\n   - The actor fetches with the cookie-less fetcher, from forum-images hosts only.\n   - It honours the image policy (LOT-107), caps the file size, and skips the download when the cache is fresh (24 h).\n   - MP rows reload when the store reports a new avatar: add the store's generation to the row's `.task(id:)`.\n2. **Monogram placeholder.** Initials on a disc whose colour comes from a stable hash of the pseudo, with ≥4.5:1 text contrast. This replaces the grey disc; groups keep their icon.\n3. **Later (needs a capture):** prefetch from profiles for correspondents never opened. This needs the `profilebdd.php?pseudo=` redirect captured (pending capture in HFR-PROTOCOL); open a `host: mac` capture issue then. No guessing.\n\n### Acceptance\n- Tests with a loopback-only session: no cookie is sent, and the policy is respected.\n- A row refreshes after a store write.\n- The monogram is deterministic.\n- Mac check: light, dark, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type XL.\n- A GAP row records the monogram.\n\nRouting: Sonnet 5.5 → Opus 5.5, effort M plus S. Part of the visual consistency umbrella.",
